{
  "_comment": "The mountain map, top (summit, z small) to bottom. Map coords: x -10..10, z 0..mapDepth. Each region is a band z0..z1 with a ground tile while critter-held and once conquered. Nodes: cafe (go home), battle (an outpost: rooms of the region's critters), boss (needs every battle node of the region beaten; beating it conquers the region), lot (a branch shop, buyable once the region is conquered). A region opens when the one above is conquered. secrets = hidden off the path, shown when the cat is near: chest (coin, once), patch (an ingredient, regrows daily; fish goes to a barrel), lostcat (that cat joins the household, once). patrols = critters wandering the region until it is conquered. layers (optional, else rooms fights) = the dungeon run: room kinds per layer, a door per option (battle.json); name = what the HUD calls the node. intro = said the first time the cat walks in. decor = hand-placed props (kind, x, z, active). ambient = wandering critters. arenaDecor = the camp around this region's battle arena, in room coordinates (the room is 16 x 11 round 0,0). All of these are laid out with the level editor (F2). scenery = decoration kinds scattered over the band (placeholder shapes until map sheets land). enemies/boss are keys in battle.json. market = goods the market sells once this region is yours. decor active: night, sometimes, or wild (now and then, only while the region is held). room: the look of its battle rooms: two floor tiles inside (patched), edge along the rim, out beyond; border kinds ring the rim (low kinds on the south rim so they never hide the cat), fill kinds crowd the dark beyond (dimmed by dark), decor props (sheets) stand just outside, obstacles grow inside.",
